{
  "part": {
    "name": "Elongated mounting arm with blind cylindrical socket",
    "description": "Single-piece solid comprising a long rectangular rail with a rounded terminal, a locally enlarged blended support, and a hollow cylindrical boss oriented transverse to the rail. The boss contains a blind cylindrical bore that provides a mating or locating interface.",
    "source_views": [
      "front",
      "back",
      "left",
      "right",
      "top",
      "bottom",
      "toprightiso"
    ],
    "symmetry_note": "The part is approximately mirror-symmetric about the rail mid-thickness plane z=4 mm. It is not symmetric along its length because the cylindrical socket is offset toward the rounded end and the opposite end is square."
  },
  "Section": [
    {
      "id": "SEC-01",
      "name": "Base rail",
      "features included": [
        "Long structural arm",
        "Broad upper and lower load-carrying faces",
        "Straight longitudinal side walls",
        "Square terminal interface",
        "Rounded opposite terminal",
        "Local rear-side shoulder adjacent to the socket transition"
      ],
      "function intent": "Acts as the principal mounting arm or lever body, establishes the overall span of the part, and transfers loads between the cylindrical socket region and the remote square end. The rounded end removes a sharp projecting corner and may provide clearance near adjacent components.",
      "physical behavior": "The rail behaves primarily as a beam under bending, axial loading, and possible torsion. Its broad parallel faces provide bending stiffness, while the longitudinal side walls carry shear. The rounded terminal distributes local edge stress and reduces interference compared with a square corner.",
      "geometry": "A constant-thickness elongated prismatic strip extending mainly along the x direction. It has parallel planar faces at z=2 mm and z=6 mm, straight sides at y=11 mm and y=23 mm, a square end at x=80 mm, and a large cylindrical arc forming the opposite end. The rear side is interrupted locally by the socket transition.",
      "location": "Extends across the full length of the part from the rounded end at x=-25 mm to the square end at x=80 mm, below and forward of the cylindrical socket.",
      "colour": {
        "R": 70,
        "G": 130,
        "B": 180
      },
      "major_faces": [
        {
          "face_code": "0000",
          "name": "Front longitudinal wall",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 5",
          "description": "Long planar side wall at y=11 mm spanning the full rail length."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0001",
          "name": "Square terminal face",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 7",
          "description": "Rectangular planar end face at x=80 mm forming the remote square termination of the rail."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0002",
          "name": "Lower broad face",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 1",
          "description": "Large planar rail face at z=2 mm, bounded by the straight sides, square end, rounded end, and socket-region interruptions."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0003",
          "name": "Rounded terminal wall",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 0",
          "description": "Cylindrical curved side patch of radius 17.5 mm forming the rounded left terminal of the constant-thickness rail."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0004",
          "name": "Local rear shoulder",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 2",
          "description": "Small planar patch at y=23 mm between the rounded terminal and the blended socket support."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0005",
          "name": "Upper broad face",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 6",
          "description": "Large planar rail face at z=6 mm providing the opposite broad surface from the lower face."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0006",
          "name": "Rear longitudinal wall",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 8",
          "description": "Long planar side wall at y=23 mm extending from the socket-transition region to the square terminal."
        }
      ],
      "minor_faces_Brep_id": [],
      "relationships": [
        {
          "source id": "SEC-01",
          "target id": "SEC-02",
          "function relationship": "transmits_load; distributes_stress; supports",
          "structural relationship": "attached_to; shares_face; blends_into"
        },
        {
          "source id": "SEC-01",
          "target id": "SEC-03",
          "function relationship": "supports; offset_from_socket_axis; provides_clearance",
          "structural relationship": "attached_to; offset_from"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SEC-02",
      "name": "Blended socket support",
      "features included": [
        "Bulbous transition",
        "Socket-to-rail junction",
        "Stress-distributing blend",
        "Local reinforcement around the cylindrical boss"
      ],
      "function intent": "Joins the cylindrical socket to the thin rail without an abrupt right-angle intersection. It reinforces the mounting point and spreads loads from the boss into a wider area of the rail.",
      "physical behavior": "The continuously curved transition reduces stress concentration at the boss root. Under radial, bending, or torsional loading of the socket, it converts concentrated boss-wall loads into distributed membrane, shear, and bending loads in the base rail.",
      "geometry": "A non-analytic bulbous B-spline surface centered around x=0 and z=4 mm. It occupies approximately y=19 to 24 mm and expands to about 14 mm across x and z, blending the rail side and broad faces into the outer cylindrical boss.",
      "location": "At the root of the cylindrical socket, centered near x=0 on the rear side of the base rail and partially wrapping above and below the rail thickness.",
      "colour": {
        "R": 238,
        "G": 140,
        "B": 50
      },
      "major_faces": [
        {
          "face_code": "0007",
          "name": "Bulbous root blend",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 9",
          "description": "Continuous B-spline transition surface joining the base rail to the outer wall of the cylindrical socket."
        }
      ],
      "minor_faces_Brep_id": [],
      "relationships": [
        {
          "source id": "SEC-02",
          "target id": "SEC-01",
          "function relationship": "transmits_load; distributes_stress",
          "structural relationship": "blends_into; attached_to"
        },
        {
          "source id": "SEC-02",
          "target id": "SEC-03",
          "function relationship": "supports; transmits_load; constrains_dof",
          "structural relationship": "attached_to; blends_into; coaxial_with"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "SEC-03",
      "name": "Blind cylindrical socket",
      "features included": [
        "Outer cylindrical boss",
        "Annular opening rim",
        "Blind cylindrical bore",
        "Planar bore floor",
        "Mating-part locating interface"
      ],
      "function intent": "Provides a transverse cylindrical mounting or locating interface for insertion of a pin, shaft, post, or mating cylindrical component. The annular end supports entry and axial seating, while the blind bore limits insertion depth.",
      "physical behavior": "The outer cylindrical wall resists radial contact pressure, bending, and hoop stress. The inner bore locates a mating cylinder and constrains transverse translation. The planar bore floor provides an axial stop, and the annular rim carries local end contact while maintaining material around the opening.",
      "geometry": "A hollow cylindrical boss centered at x=0 and z=4 mm with its axis along the y direction. The outer radius is 7 mm and extends approximately from y=24 to 34 mm. The bore radius is 5 mm and extends from the open end at y=34 mm to a closed planar floor at y=25 mm.",
      "location": "Centered over the blended support near x=0, projecting from the rear side of the rail toward y=34 mm.",
      "colour": {
        "R": 80,
        "G": 180,
        "B": 105
      },
      "major_faces": [
        {
          "face_code": "0008",
          "name": "Outer boss cylinder",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 10",
          "description": "External cylindrical wall of radius 7 mm forming the main body of the socket boss."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0009",
          "name": "Annular opening face",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 11",
          "description": "Planar annulus at y=34 mm surrounding the open end of the blind bore."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0010",
          "name": "Inner bore cylinder",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 3",
          "description": "Cylindrical internal locating surface of radius 5 mm extending inward from the open end."
        },
        {
          "face_code": "0011",
          "name": "Blind bore floor",
          "Brep_id": "FACE 4",
          "description": "Circular planar face at y=25 mm closing the bore and providing an axial insertion stop."
        }
      ],
      "minor_faces_Brep_id": [],
      "relationships": [
        {
          "source id": "SEC-03",
          "target id": "SEC-02",
          "function relationship": "transmits_load; mounts_to; constrains_dof",
          "structural relationship": "attached_to; blends_into; coaxial_with"
        },
        {
          "source id": "SEC-03",
          "target id": "SEC-01",
          "function relationship": "locates_mating_part; transmits_load; provides_clearance",
          "structural relationship": "supported_by; offset_from"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}
